      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Printed as a bracketed classification: a group name in the left margin, braces grouping peoples, and braces grouping peoples against a region. Each people is given its own row; a region shared by a brace is repeated on every row it covers, and the group name is repeated on every row within its brace.",
        "Part I: Urianhai, Sok-pa and Taldi (?) are printed in the group column without a brace, and are put in 'Group' with 'People' blank. The Turki Family (top of p. 29) continues Part I.",
        "Part I: the right-hand brace for 'S., E. and S.E. Mongolia' spans Uchumsin…Naiman; 'N. bend of the Huang-ho' is printed level with Ordos, at the foot of that brace.",
        "Part III: 'extinct ?' is printed with a brace against Chimpan and Khato-zun; put in 'Division'.",
        "Part IV: one right-hand brace spans Pe-Lolo…Sen-Lolo, with two regions printed against it ('S. bend of the Yangtze' / 'S. Szechuan, N. Yunnan'); it is not shown which people go with which, so both are given (joined by '; ') on all four rows.",
        "Part IV: 'Chung, Nguchung, Tu-man, Kilao, Kitao' is one bracketed entry hyphenated across a line break; joined as 'Tuman'. Similarly 'Tanguts (Northern Ti-betans)' joined.",
        "Part IV continues on p. 30 (Pagni … Shuk-lai) under the same heading."
      ],
